/- An oracle test: a program + its expected output from bpref.py.
The 121 oracle programs live in bench/oracles/ (121 scripts).
This declares the full list of oracle entries with their bpref values.
Values are taken from the oracle scripts in bench/oracles/.
-/
structure OracleEntry where
  name : String
  source : String       -- .bp source text
  bprefResult : Val     -- what bpref.py returns for this program
  deriving Inhabited

/- 97 program entries: the VERBATIM `.bp` source of each program, with the
EXPECT value it is checked against.

MEASURED AND REPAIRED 2026-09-14 (lane l4lean). Almost every `source` string
in this array used to be an INVENTED program that was never the file it names.
Counted mechanically against the real files (whitespace- and comment-
normalised): 96 of these 97 names have a real `.bp` in the tree -- 76 under
`bench/parity_constructs/`, 20 under `bench/vs_rust/std_tests/` -- and only
**8 of those 96** carried that file's actual text (7 parity constructs and
`attn`). **88 were fabricated.** The tell was that some of them are
not even in the language: `c05_if` read
  fn main() -> i64 { let x = 10; if x > 5 { 111 } else { 0 } }
with brace arms, while Bebop's `if` is `if c then a else b` (LANGUAGE.md:75),
so that string could never compile. `c02_arith` read `a + b * 2` = 16 against
EXPECT 34 -- the same mis-transcription that was already found and fixed in
`sample_c02` below, still sitting here unfixed because the two were never
cross-checked. Others simply disagreed with themselves: `c08_call` was
`add(3,4)` against 6, `c14_string` was `str_len("hello")` against 8,
`c10_struct` summed 3+4 against 11, `c22_matchbind` returned 42 against 7,
`c96_enumpay` computed 10020030 against 8503009.

The VALUES were fine: all 76 parity rows agreed with the `// EXPECT` line of
the real .bp (0 disagreements), so only the sources were wrong. The 20
std_tests .bp files carry no `// EXPECT` line, so their values are unchecked
by this comparison. Each `source` below is now the byte-for-byte
content of `bench/parity_constructs/<name>.bp`, or of
`bench/vs_rust/std_tests/<name>.bp` for the 20 std_test programs, read and
substituted by script rather than retyped. `crc32` (1 row) has no `.bp` file
anywhere in the tree -- it is a bench/oracles/*.py-only entry -- and keeps its
hand-written one-liner, flagged here so it is not mistaken for a real file.

NOTE ON THE COUNT: the header of this file says "121 oracle program entries"
and `oracleCount` below still says 121. This array holds 97. The 121 figure is
the ROADMAP F4 target, not a measurement of this array. -/
def oracleEntries : Array OracleEntry := #[
  -- c01_lit: integer literals and wrapping
  ⟨"c01_lit", "// literals: small, big, negative-computed\n// EXPECT 1000000065571 from: hand: 42 + 65536 + 1000000000000 + (0 - 7)\nfn main() -> i64 { 42 + 65536 + 1000000000000 + (0 - 7) }", 1000000065571⟩,
  -- c02_arith: arithmetic operators
  ⟨"c02_arith", "// arithmetic: + - * / %\n// EXPECT 34 from: hand: 20 + 22 - 2*5/2 - 7%4 = 42 - 5 - 3 (note re-derived 2026-09-13 from the program below; it said 10 + 2*3 + 8/2, which is 20 and was what a Lean encoding transcribed)\nfn main() -> i64 { 20 + 22 - 2 * 5 / 2 - 7 % 4 }", 34⟩,
  -- c03_precedence: operator precedence
  ⟨"c03_precedence", "// precedence + nesting\n// EXPECT 7 from: hand: 3 + 4 (multiplication before addition)\nfn main() -> i64 { 2 * (3 + 4) - (10 - 3) * 2 + 1 + 2 * 3 }", 7⟩,
  -- c04_cmp: comparisons
  ⟨"c04_cmp", "// comparisons\n// EXPECT 310 from: hand: sum of comparison results\nfn main() -> i64 {\n  let a = if 1 < 2 then 10 else 0;\n  let b = if 3 >= 3 then 20 else 0;\n  let c = if 2 > 3 then 0 else 40;\n  let d = if 1 == 1 then 80 else 0;\n  let e = if 1 != 2 then 160 else 0;\n  a + b + c + d + e\n}", 310⟩,
  -- c05_if: if-then-else
  ⟨"c05_if", "// if/then/else + nested\n// EXPECT 111 from: hand: if-else conditional\nfn main() -> i64 { if 5 > 3 then (if 2 > 1 then 111 else 0) else 222 }", 111⟩,
  -- c06_let: let bindings
  ⟨"c06_let", "// lets + shadow updates\n// EXPECT 7 from: hand: let binding\nfn main() -> i64 {\n  let acc = 0;\n  let acc = acc + 1;\n  let acc = acc + 2;\n  let acc = acc + 4;\n  acc\n}", 7⟩,
  -- c07_while: while loop
  ⟨"c07_while", "// while loop\n// EXPECT 45 from: hand: sum from 1 to 9 (while loop)\nfn main() -> i64 {\n  let i = 0;\n  let acc = 0;\n  while i < 10 {\n    let acc = acc + i;\n    let i = i + 1;\n    0\n  };\n  acc\n}", 45⟩,
  -- c08_call: function call
  ⟨"c08_call", "// cross-fn call\n// EXPECT 6 from: hand: function call\nfn main() -> i64 { add3(1, 2, 3) }\nfn add3(a: i64, b: i64, c: i64) -> i64 { a + b + c }", 6⟩,
