  ⟨"csr", "use \"selfhost/prelude/fp.bp\"\n// (T47c 2026-09-05: was `// prelude: fp`; the expansion used to be textual via tools/gen_selfsrc.sh)\n// csr.bp — structural twin of dowiz/core/src/csr.rs (golden: CSR GOLDENS\n// section in bench/vs_rust/spectral_golden/golden.txt).\n// CSR layout: rp[n+1] row offsets, ci[nnz] column indices ascending within\n// each row, vv[nnz] weights in 2^32 fixed-point (fp(1.0) = 4294967296).\n// from_edges contract mirrored exactly: per-row buckets in input order,\n// stable sort by column, adjacent duplicate columns MERGED by summing\n// weights (wrapping i64 addition is commutative — merge result exact),\n// edges with src/dst out of range ignored. Working buffer caps m <= 4096.\n// LAW: cross-loop state lives in CELLS ([0] buffers), never in plain rebinds\n// — the two engines disagree on rebind visibility across loop nests.\n\n// fp_mul(a,b): (a*b) >> 32 — schoolbook 32-bit split (see spectral.bp; the\n// same exact-64-bit schoolbook, duplicated so csr.bp stays standalone).\n// Bebop >> is LOGICAL (u64) on both engines: split on magnitudes, fold sign.\n\n// csr_from_edges(n, es, ed, ew, m, rp, ci, vv): m edges (src,dst,weight-fp).\n// rp needs n+1 cells, ci/vv need <= m cells (<= 4096 edges). Returns nnz.\nfn csr_from_edges(n: i64, es: [i64], ed: [i64], ew: [i64], m: i64, rp: [i64], ci: [i64], vv: [i64]) -> i64 {\n  let wcol = zeros(4096);\n  let wval = zeros(4096);\n  let nnzc = zeros(1);\n  let wcnt = zeros(1);\n  let mcell = zeros(1);\n  let tc = zeros(1);\n  let pcol = zeros(1);\n  let i = 0;\n  while i < n {\n    let _ = wcnt[0] = 0;\n    let e = 0;\n    while e < m {\n      let src = es[e];\n      let dst = ed[e];\n      let ok = (if src == i then 1 else 0) * (if src < n then 1 else 0) * (if dst < n then 1 else 0);\n      let _ = if ok == 1 then (let _ = wcol[wcnt[0]] = dst in (let _ = wval[wcnt[0]] = ew[e] in (let _ = wcnt[0] = wcnt[0] + 1 in 0))) else 0;\n      let e = e + 1;\n      0\n    };\n    // selection sort by co